---
import CodeTabs from '../../components/CodeTabs.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="GET /getLyrics">
  <p class="endpoint-badge">
    <span class="method">GET</span>
    <code>/getLyrics</code>
  </p>

  <p><a class="try-it" href="/playground?s=APT.&a=ROS%C3%89%2C+Bruno+Mars&al=APT.&d=170">Try it in the playground</a></p>

  <p>
    Fetch synced lyrics for a song, with syllable-level timing in TTML format.
  </p>

  <h2>Parameters</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Name</th>
        <th>Type</th>
        <th>Required</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>s</code>, <code>song</code>, <code>songName</code></td>
        <td>string</td>
        <td>At least one of song or artist</td>
        <td>Song title</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>a</code>, <code>artist</code>, <code>artistName</code></td>
        <td>string</td>
        <td>At least one of song or artist</td>
        <td>Artist name</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>al</code>, <code>album</code>, <code>albumName</code></td>
        <td>string</td>
        <td>No</td>
        <td>Album name (improves matching)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>d</code>, <code>duration</code></td>
        <td>string of digits</td>
        <td>No</td>
        <td>Track duration in whole seconds, for example <code>242</code> (improves matching)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>videoId</code>, <code>v</code></td>
        <td>string</td>
        <td>No</td>
        <td>Video ID of the track. It is stored with the song so that downstream caches can be refreshed. It does not change matching.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note">
    If you send more than one alias of a parameter (for example <code>s</code> and <code>song</code>),
    the values are joined together. Send only one alias of each.
  </p>

  <h2>Headers</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Name</th>
        <th>Required</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-API-Key</code></td>
        <td>Conditional</td>
        <td>Needed for cache misses when the server enforces API keys. A valid key also skips rate limiting.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Example request</h2>
  <CodeTabs tabs={[
    { language: 'curl', code: `curl "https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=Shape%20of%20You&a=Ed%20Sheeran&d=234"` },
    { language: 'javascript', code: `const res = await fetch("https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=Shape%20of%20You&a=Ed%20Sheeran&d=234");
const { ttml } = await res.json();` },
    { language: 'python', code: `import requests

res = requests.get("https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=Shape%20of%20You&a=Ed%20Sheeran&d=234")
ttml = res.json()["ttml"]` },
    { language: 'go', code: `package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"io"
	"net/http"
)

func main() {
	res, err := http.Get("https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=Shape%20of%20You&a=Ed%20Sheeran&d=234")
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	defer res.Body.Close()

	body, err := io.ReadAll(res.Body)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	fmt.Println(string(body))
}` },
  ]} />

  <h2>Success response</h2>
  <p>Status: <code>200 OK</code>, <code>Content-Type: application/json</code></p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "ttml": "<?xml version=\\"1.0\\" encoding=\\"UTF-8\\"?>\\n<tt xmlns=\\"http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml\\">\\n  <body>\\n    <div>\\n      <p begin=\\"00:00:18.234\\" end=\\"00:00:21.891\\">\\n        <span begin=\\"00:00:18.234\\" end=\\"00:00:18.567\\">The </span>\\n        ...\\n      </p>\\n    </div>\\n  </body>\\n</tt>",
  "score": 0.97
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Response fields</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Field</th>
        <th>Type</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>ttml</code></td>
        <td>string</td>
        <td>The TTML document</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>score</code></td>
        <td>number</td>
        <td>
          Match confidence from <code>0</code> to <code>1</code>. Sent only when the lyrics were fetched
          for this request, or when the request joined a fetch for the same query that was already in progress.
          Cache hits and <code>STALE</code> responses have only <code>ttml</code>.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Response headers</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Header</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-Cache-Status</code></td>
        <td><code>HIT</code>, <code>MISS</code>, <code>NEGATIVE_HIT</code>, or <code>STALE</code>. A request that joined a fetch already in progress gets <code>HIT</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-RateLimit-Limit</code></td>
        <td>Burst size of the current rate limit tier. Not sent with a valid API key.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-RateLimit-Remaining</code></td>
        <td>Requests left in the current tier. Not sent with a valid API key.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-RateLimit-Type</code></td>
        <td><code>normal</code>, <code>cached</code>, <code>exceeded</code>, or <code>bypass</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-RateLimit-Bypass</code></td>
        <td><code>true</code> when a valid API key skipped rate limiting</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-Auth-Mode</code></td>
        <td><code>authenticated</code>, <code>invalid</code>, or <code>cache</code>. Sent only when the server enforces API keys.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Retry-After</code></td>
        <td>Seconds to wait. Only on <code>429</code> responses.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    <code>/getLyrics</code> does not send <code>X-Provider</code>. See
    <a href="#provider-specific-endpoints">Provider-specific endpoints</a> for the endpoints that do.
  </p>

  <h2>Error responses</h2>
  <p>All error responses are JSON, except <code>422</code> and the <code>429</code> sent when both rate limit tiers are exhausted, which are plain text.</p>

  <h3>Missing parameters (422)</h3>
  <p>Sent when neither song nor artist is given. <code>Content-Type: text/plain</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>Song name or artist name not provided</code></pre>

  <h3>API key required (401)</h3>
  <p>The query is not cached, the server enforces API keys, and the request has no key:</p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "API key required",
  "message": "Uncached queries require a valid API key via X-API-Key header"
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>With a wrong key:</p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "Invalid API key",
  "message": "The provided API key is not valid"
}`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Not found (404)</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "Lyrics not available for this track"
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    The <code>error</code> text depends on why no lyrics were found. This result is cached, and later
    requests for the same query get <code>X-Cache-Status: NEGATIVE_HIT</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>Rate limited (429)</h3>
  <p>
    Both rate limit tiers are exhausted. <code>Content-Type: text/plain</code>,
    <code>Retry-After: 1</code>, <code>X-RateLimit-Type: exceeded</code>:
  </p>
  <pre><code>Too Many Requests</code></pre>
  <p>
    The normal tier is exhausted and the query is not cached, so the cached tier cannot serve it.
    JSON, <code>Retry-After: 60</code>, <code>X-RateLimit-Type: cached</code>:
  </p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "Rate limit exceeded. This request requires cached data, but no cache is available for this query.",
  "message": "Please try again later or reduce your request rate."
}`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Upstream error (500)</h3>
  <p>The upstream fetch failed and no cached fallback exists. The <code>error</code> text is the upstream error:</p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "<upstream error message>"
}`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Cache-only mode (503)</h3>
  <p>The server is temporarily serving only cached lyrics and the query is not cached:</p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "Service running in cache-only mode. No cached lyrics available for this query."
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2 id="provider-specific-endpoints">Provider-specific endpoints</h2>
  <p>
    These endpoints select one provider. They take the same <code>s</code>, <code>a</code>, <code>al</code>
    and <code>d</code> parameters (but not <code>videoId</code>), and return the same <code>422</code> and
    rate limit responses.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Endpoint</th>
        <th>Format</th>
        <th>Timing</th>
        <th>API key for cache misses</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>/ttml/getLyrics</code></td>
        <td>TTML</td>
        <td>Syllable-level</td>
        <td>When the server enforces API keys</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>/kugou/getLyrics</code></td>
        <td>LRC-style text</td>
        <td>Line-level</td>
        <td>Never</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>/qq/getLyrics</code></td>
        <td><a href="/docs/qrc-format">QRC</a></td>
        <td>Word-level</td>
        <td>Never</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "lyrics": "<?xml version=\\"1.0\\" encoding=\\"UTF-8\\"?>...",
  "provider": "ttml"
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>They differ from <code>/getLyrics</code> in these ways:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The body is <code>lyrics</code> and <code>provider</code>, not <code>ttml</code>. There is no <code>score</code>.</li>
    <li>Every JSON response, errors included, has an <code>X-Provider</code> header with the provider name. JSON error bodies also have a <code>provider</code> field.</li>
    <li>Cache lookups use the exact cache key. There is no duration tolerance and no <code>STALE</code> fallback.</li>
    <li>
      <code>/ttml/getLyrics</code> builds its cache keys in a different format from <code>/getLyrics</code>. When you send an
      album or a duration, the two endpoints do not share cache entries.
    </li>
    <li><code>X-Auth-Mode</code> is sent only by <code>/ttml/getLyrics</code>, and only when the server enforces API keys.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
